  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Kollipara Akhil Kumar vs The State Of Andhra Pradesh on 5 September, 2019 Author: U. Durga Prasad Rao Bench: U. Durga Prasad Rao Hon'Ble Sri Justice U. Durga Prasad Rao Criminal Petition No.4722 Of 2019 Order:",
    "facts": "The petitioners/A1 and A2 seek to quash the proceedings against them in Crime No.107 of 2019 of Atchempeta Police Station, Guntur District, registered for the offences under Sections 188, 272, 273 and 420 of IPC and Sections 58, 59 and 63 of Food Safety and Standards Act (for short, 'FSS Act'). 2. The allegations against the petitioners briefly are that on 26.04.2019 at 11.00 A.M., when the complainant inspected the Ramakrishna Cool Drinks Shop situated at Kothari Centre, Atchmepeta, found the banned tobacco products and on interrogation, as the accused confessed to have been engaged in the business of prohibited tobacco products, seized the same, registered F.I.R. for the offences stated supra. 3.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for petitioners while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore, the police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore, registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for petitioners while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore, the police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore, registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
